  "Question": "Chickens and rabbits are in the same cage, with a total of 35 heads and 94 legs. Let there be \\(x\\) chickens and \\(y\\) rabbits. Which system of equations is correct?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\begin{cases}x+y=35\\\\4x+2y=94\\end{cases}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\begin{cases}x+y=35\\\\2x+4y=94\\end{cases}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\begin{cases}x+y=94\\\\2x+4y=35\\end{cases}\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The total number of heads gives \\(x+y=35\\). Each chicken has 2 legs and each rabbit has 4 legs, so the total number of legs gives \\(2x+4y=94\\).",
